00:20:03.290 --> 00:20:03.950
Excuse me, Pa.

00:20:06.510 --> 00:20:08.490
Speaking of decoration...

00:20:08.490 --> 00:20:09.270
Hear, hear.

00:20:11.180 --> 00:20:14.090
Ellie, I didn't know you were back in town.

00:20:15.160 --> 00:20:16.350
You never looked.

00:20:18.580 --> 00:20:21.310
You surprised me tonight, Colonel Casey.

00:20:22.150 --> 00:20:25.140
The voice of reason coming out of the military man.

00:20:25.570 --> 00:20:26.840
Got a lot of hidden talents.

00:20:26.840 --> 00:20:29.220
Oh, I suspected that right along.

00:20:30.220 --> 00:20:32.180
Ever since my ex-lover introduced us.

00:20:33.290 --> 00:20:37.090
And how is the staunch General Scott and his lovely wife?

00:20:37.290 --> 00:20:38.190
Well, he keeps busy.

00:20:38.670 --> 00:20:39.550
So I read.

00:20:40.160 --> 00:20:45.540
There's a sizable portion of the citizenry who says that he's the savior of the Western world.

00:20:45.850 --> 00:20:46.950
Does his job, Ellie.

00:20:47.900 --> 00:20:49.320
Well, take care of him, Jiggs.

00:20:49.840 --> 00:20:51.760
See that he rests on the seventh day.

00:20:52.130 --> 00:20:52.630
I'll try.

00:20:56.320 --> 00:20:58.100
Marvelous military stoicism.

00:20:59.000 --> 00:21:00.000
The Iron Man.

00:21:01.210 --> 00:21:03.470
Is that for quenching a torch or washing out a wound?

00:21:06.120 --> 00:21:08.180
Well, let me put it to you this way, Jigs, darling.

00:21:09.210 --> 00:21:11.410
What the hell business is it of yours?

00:21:12.120 --> 00:21:14.390
I want that.

00:21:14.530 --> 00:21:15.110
No, you don't.

00:21:17.900 --> 00:21:21.040
You listen to me.

00:21:21.120 --> 00:21:21.860
Now, what is it?

00:21:22.460 --> 00:21:23.730
Is it just Scott?

00:21:25.660 --> 00:21:26.100
Scott.

00:21:26.300 --> 00:21:27.060
Scott and everything.

00:21:27.650 --> 00:21:30.000
That's my own.

00:21:30.380 --> 00:21:36.120
life not the first name to ever wind up on the bottom of the deck that happens every day what

00:21:36.120 --> 00:21:41.370
matters is how a person lives with it stop playing the part of the anguished drunk digging olives

00:21:41.370 --> 00:21:48.460
out of martinis and boring everybody with tragic stories you know sober ellie you're a bright

00:21:48.460 --> 00:22:00.000
beautiful day good to have around will you drive me home jigs whatever you say

00:22:08.030 --> 00:22:10.480
"Good night, Stu. Thank you for a very nice party."

00:22:10.480 --> 00:22:12.980
"Thanks for coming, Senator. Real pleasure having you."

00:22:12.980 --> 00:22:17.100
"Oh, Jiggs. Jiggs, I hope you forgive my little outburst tonight."

00:22:17.100 --> 00:22:21.080
"The combination of deep concerns and dry martinis, that can be a dangerous combo."

00:22:21.080 --> 00:22:22.900
"I've been reamed by experts, Senator."

00:22:22.900 --> 00:22:24.320
"Great summer."

00:22:24.320 --> 00:22:30.000
"Oh, look, Colonel Casey, I was simply trying to get you to say what I happen to know you believe."

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:36.980
You're working for the one man who commands confidence who could possibly lead us out of this mess.

00:22:36.980 --> 00:22:41.770
You just remember, there are plenty of us up on the hill who stand right alongside of you.

00:22:41.770 --> 00:22:47.510
You've all got to stay on the alert these days, Casey.

00:22:47.510 --> 00:22:50.080
Especially on Sunday, right?

00:23:18.040 --> 00:23:20.240
I've got to drive out to Fort Myer to see the general.

00:23:21.680 --> 00:23:23.360
May I call a cab for you?

00:23:23.920 --> 00:23:24.900
No, thank you. I'll manage.

00:23:25.540 --> 00:23:27.560
I'm sorry, Ellie, but this is very important.

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:34.230
But just in case someone forgets to mention it, you're a great crutch.

00:23:34.230 --> 00:23:39.660
It's too bad you're only available 20 minutes at a time.

00:23:39.660 --> 00:23:43.160
Well, you can't tell. Sometimes the country can spare me for a whole evening.

00:23:43.160 --> 00:23:49.080
Give me a rain shake and I'll prove it.

00:23:49.080 --> 00:23:52.310
Tuck it somewhere safe, where you won't forget it.

00:23:52.310 --> 00:23:55.070
Good night, Ellie.

00:23:55.070 --> 00:23:56.630
Good night, Jicks.

00:25:17.080 --> 00:25:18.080
Hi, Jack.

00:25:18.080 --> 00:25:20.850
Hi, Jukes.

00:25:20.850 --> 00:25:21.220
Colonel Lubbock's with him.

00:25:35.850 --> 00:25:43.210
my favorite jarhead himself jigs casey hello broderick i thought you'd be in okinawa or maybe

00:25:43.210 --> 00:25:50.100
worse ah not me casey boy not me still protecting the great unwashed i thought you'd be a civil

00:25:50.100 --> 00:25:57.760
liberties lawyer by now you might make it yet you might make it yet by the way casey my boy

00:25:57.760 --> 00:26:00.000
i hear you're doing a fine job as director for the joint chiefs

00:26:00.090 --> 00:26:04.450
- Fine job.

00:26:04.450 --> 00:26:06.350
- Hello, Jiggs.

00:26:06.350 --> 00:26:08.120
- Morning, sir.

00:26:08.120 --> 00:26:09.720
- How was the party last night?

00:26:09.720 --> 00:26:12.280
- You missed a good one.

00:26:12.280 --> 00:26:13.630
- Anyone there I know?

00:26:13.630 --> 00:26:15.530
- Well, Paul Girard from the White House

00:26:15.530 --> 00:26:19.180
and, oh, Senator Prentiss were the ranking guests.

00:26:19.180 --> 00:26:20.060
- With those two, there must have been

00:26:20.060 --> 00:26:21.300
quite a hassle over the treaty.

00:26:21.300 --> 00:26:23.290
- There was, sir.

00:26:23.290 --> 00:26:25.760
- Prentiss up hold our side all right?

00:26:25.760 --> 00:26:26.620
- Pretty candid.

00:26:26.620 --> 00:26:28.870
Also quite complimentary about you.

00:26:30.000 --> 00:26:33.070
- By the way, Ellie Holbrook was there.

00:26:33.070 --> 00:26:38.250
It was nice seeing her again.

00:26:38.250 --> 00:26:39.590
- Let's get on with it, Jigs.

00:26:39.590 --> 00:26:41.670
- Yes, sir.

00:26:41.670 --> 00:26:45.640
Now, these are from January's All Red Alert, sir.

00:26:45.640 --> 00:26:48.520
Pearl Harbor, 12 minutes after the threat warning.

00:26:48.520 --> 00:26:51.080
- 12 minutes, and over 80% of the fleet

00:26:51.080 --> 00:26:54.230
still sitting there like overfed ducks.

00:26:54.230 --> 00:26:54.800
- Next.

00:27:00.000 --> 00:27:02.970
- Right field, 22 minutes into the alert.

00:27:02.970 --> 00:27:05.330
- This one really gives me an ache in the gut.

00:27:05.330 --> 00:27:07.250
Half those aircraft aren't even scrambled,

00:27:07.250 --> 00:27:12.860
let alone off the ground.

00:27:12.860 --> 00:27:15.980
- Over Mount Thunder.

00:27:15.980 --> 00:27:17.780
The President's in the middle helicopter.

00:27:17.780 --> 00:27:19.180
- Right out in the open.

00:27:19.180 --> 00:27:21.080
- 34 minutes into the alert.

00:27:21.080 --> 00:27:23.440
Can sound indicates possibility of hostile action

00:27:23.440 --> 00:27:24.580
by the Soviet Union.

00:27:30.000 --> 00:27:31.000
30 more shots, sir.

00:27:31.530 --> 00:27:32.290
Each one of them

00:27:32.290 --> 00:27:32.890
more followed up

00:27:32.890 --> 00:27:33.390
than the others.

00:27:34.480 --> 00:27:35.910
Well, let's hope

00:27:35.910 --> 00:27:36.530
Sunday's alert

00:27:36.530 --> 00:27:37.290
will be different, sir.

00:27:38.210 --> 00:27:39.170
That damn well better be.

00:27:40.800 --> 00:27:44.860
Sir, wouldn't it help

00:27:44.860 --> 00:27:46.280
if you changed your mind

00:27:46.280 --> 00:27:47.060
and, uh...

00:27:47.060 --> 00:27:47.720
About what, Jiggs?

00:27:49.140 --> 00:27:49.800
I invited some

00:27:49.800 --> 00:27:50.580
of the congressional people

00:27:50.580 --> 00:27:51.380
to observe the alert.

00:27:54.230 --> 00:27:55.210
Well, it wouldn't hurt us

00:27:55.210 --> 00:27:56.110
if a congressman

00:27:56.110 --> 00:27:56.590
or a senator

00:27:56.590 --> 00:27:57.450
saw how effectively

00:27:57.450 --> 00:27:58.290
we can work

00:27:58.290 --> 00:27:58.950
when we have to.

00:27:59.200 --> 00:28:00.000
Nobody from the hills

00:28:00.000 --> 00:28:10.410
to know a thing about this yes sir yes it's 9 20 sir they're waiting for you in the conference room

00:28:10.410 --> 00:28:15.260
thank you i've even persuaded the president to come down without the press

00:28:15.260 --> 00:28:30.000
no newspaper man none get to bed late sir got to bed

00:28:30.000 --> 00:28:41.650
too early. Slept from 8 to 8. Too much sleep. I may never wake up. Stay close, Jigs. I want to see you after this meeting.

00:29:09.820 --> 00:29:14.560
Oh, Jiggs, Murdoch tells him you've heard about our pretense pool.

00:29:17.070 --> 00:29:18.370
Keep it to yourself.

00:29:19.110 --> 00:29:20.270
All I want is the right horse.

00:29:21.960 --> 00:29:27.520
With Admiral Bondswell's reply, I'd appreciate that if you'd keep that in confidence, too.

00:29:27.840 --> 00:29:28.230
Of course.

00:29:31.530 --> 00:29:32.790
See, the Navy wasn't here today.

00:29:34.660 --> 00:29:36.470
Palmer couldn't make it. We're briefly later.

00:29:37.590 --> 00:29:39.070
Speaking of the Navy, that reminds me.

00:29:39.850 --> 00:29:41.950
That young J.G. in all-service radio.

00:29:42.010 --> 00:29:42.530
Grayson, sir?

00:29:42.670 --> 00:29:43.030
Grayson.

00:29:43.530 --> 00:29:44.800
He's a bit of a gossip, isn't he?

00:29:45.370 --> 00:29:46.370
He means well.

00:29:47.890 --> 00:29:50.950
Well, I'm off to New York in the AVO convention.

00:29:52.080 --> 00:29:53.630
If you get a chance, Jiggs, listen in.

00:29:54.350 --> 00:29:55.450
I'd like to know what you think about him.

00:29:55.590 --> 00:29:56.230
Certainly, sir.

00:29:56.800 --> 00:29:57.530
Good luck.

00:29:57.730 --> 00:29:58.290
Thank you.

00:30:30.220 --> 00:30:33.820
- What is it, Grayson?

00:30:33.820 --> 00:30:35.740
- Transfer.

00:30:35.740 --> 00:30:36.780
- Pearl Harbor?

00:30:36.780 --> 00:30:37.520
- Yeah.

00:30:37.520 --> 00:30:40.530
I think I got some kind of a guardian angel around here.

00:30:40.530 --> 00:30:42.390
An old Pearl Harbor.

00:30:42.390 --> 00:30:44.880
Oh, and by the way,

00:30:44.880 --> 00:30:46.040
Big Barneswell was the only one

00:30:46.040 --> 00:30:47.960
to poop out of the chairman's racing form.

00:30:47.960 --> 00:30:50.320
All the others came through with their ROUs.

00:31:14.110 --> 00:31:17.950
Ladies and gentlemen, you have heard me in my nightly newscast.

00:31:18.510 --> 00:31:19.770
You know where I stand.

00:31:20.690 --> 00:31:25.280
I'm not a lover of communists, socialists, or intellectual bleeding hearts.

00:31:25.940 --> 00:31:29.570
I happen to have only one interest, and that is symbolized...

00:31:30.090 --> 00:31:39.610
red white and blue of our glorious flag and now i'm going to give you the one man who not only

00:31:39.610 --> 00:31:44.950
speaks for that flag but has fought for it with distinction and now represents it with honor

00:31:46.480 --> 00:31:51.990
four-star general winner of the congressional medal of honor and two distinguished service

00:31:51.990 --> 00:31:59.540
crosses a hero of war a stalwart protector of the peace ladies and gentlemen

00:32:00.000 --> 00:32:08.070
The Chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff, General James Mattoon Scott!

00:32:38.320 --> 00:32:45.490
and gentlemen, members of the American Veterans Order, I would like to thank Mr. McPherson

00:32:45.490 --> 00:32:51.400
for his most laudatory comments. You're very generous, Harold. Perhaps patriotism is old

00:32:51.400 --> 00:32:58.190
fashioned. Perhaps love of country is outdated. Perhaps even a minute degree of sentiment

00:32:58.190 --> 00:33:00.000
to one's motherland is to be

00:33:00.000 --> 00:33:06.400
considered passe but God help us and God help our country if the cynics the one

00:33:06.400 --> 00:33:10.350
world is the intellectual dilettantes ever persuade us that these things have

00:33:10.350 --> 00:33:16.110
passed us by because ladies and gentlemen patriotism loyalty sentiment

00:33:16.110 --> 00:33:19.330
they are the United States of America

00:33:31.600 --> 00:33:34.900
In my lifetime, I have seen the 1,000 ways a man can die.

00:33:35.960 --> 00:33:39.960
And I know that in this country of ours, we have a perverse habit of forgetting the fact that men can't...

00:33:39.960 --> 00:33:41.780
Alfred, would you connect me to the White House, please?

00:33:42.090 --> 00:33:43.090
Or the weight...

00:34:23.320 --> 00:34:26.180
The president's expecting you, Colonel, to study second door to the right.

00:34:51.080 --> 00:34:53.080
I can tell your pals that this better be damn important.

00:34:55.050 --> 00:34:57.410
How are you, Colonel Casey?

00:34:58.020 --> 00:34:58.460
President.

00:34:59.340 --> 00:35:00.000
Please sit down.

00:35:00.730 --> 00:35:03.350
Thank you, sir.

00:35:03.350 --> 00:35:04.940
You ever been up here before, Colonel?

00:35:04.940 --> 00:35:07.790
No, sir. Big room.

00:35:07.790 --> 00:35:11.030
Too big for living and too small for convention.

00:35:11.030 --> 00:35:13.340
You want a drink, Colonel?

00:35:13.340 --> 00:35:15.030
Yes, sir. Scotch, please.

00:35:15.030 --> 00:35:17.040
Fine. I'll keep you company.

00:35:17.040 --> 00:35:20.670
- How about you, Paul? - No.

00:35:20.670 --> 00:35:27.080
And now, Colonel, that matter of national security...

00:35:33.610 --> 00:35:38.370
Mr. President, have you ever heard of a military unit known as Econ, E-Com-Con?

00:35:40.220 --> 00:35:40.720
E-what?

00:35:41.020 --> 00:35:44.500
I'm sorry, E-C-O-M-C-O-N, E-Com-Con.

00:35:48.070 --> 00:35:50.150
What does it mean?

00:35:50.510 --> 00:35:53.130
I'm not sure, sir.

00:35:55.570 --> 00:36:00.000
Well, in formal military abbreviations, it could stand for Emergency Communications Control.

00:36:03.930 --> 00:36:06.780
- I've never heard of anything like that.

00:36:06.780 --> 00:36:07.560
- Have you, Paul?

00:36:07.560 --> 00:36:08.670
- No, I haven't.

00:36:08.670 --> 00:36:09.940
- Thank you.

00:36:09.940 --> 00:36:13.470
- Well, Mr. President,

00:36:13.470 --> 00:36:15.510
have you ever authorized the formation

00:36:15.510 --> 00:36:18.960
of any type of secret unit, regardless of his name,

00:36:18.960 --> 00:36:21.750
that has something to do with the,

00:36:21.750 --> 00:36:24.150
well, preserving the security of things like

00:36:24.150 --> 00:36:26.600
television, telephone, or radio?

00:36:26.600 --> 00:36:29.600
- No, I haven't.

00:36:30.350 --> 00:36:33.260
Do you know of any secret army installation, sir,

00:36:33.300 --> 00:36:35.860
that's been set up somewhere near El Paso recently?

00:36:35.860 --> 00:36:38.750
The answer is no again. Why?

00:36:39.760 --> 00:36:43.430
Sir, this is something very difficult for me because, well,

00:36:43.530 --> 00:36:46.860
it concerns a superior officer whom I admire and respect.

00:36:46.860 --> 00:36:48.520
Well, let's get on with it, Colonel, huh?

00:36:50.020 --> 00:36:50.400
Yes, sir.

00:36:55.750 --> 00:36:58.210
Yesterday I learned from a friend of mine, Colonel Henderson,

00:36:58.370 --> 00:37:00.000
that he's the exec officer.

00:37:00.440 --> 00:37:01.200
at ComCon.

00:37:02.870 --> 00:37:04.450
Well, now, his commanding officer

00:37:04.450 --> 00:37:06.490
is an army colonel named John Broderick.

00:37:07.180 --> 00:37:08.180
Now, they're both from Signal Corps,

00:37:08.260 --> 00:37:09.400
which indicates communications.

00:37:10.370 --> 00:37:12.890
Now, they've had 100 officers

00:37:12.890 --> 00:37:15.480
and 3,600 men training secretly

00:37:15.480 --> 00:37:17.610
at a desert base near El Paso

00:37:17.610 --> 00:37:18.690
for six weeks or so.

00:37:19.800 --> 00:37:23.050
Well, then, Henderson said an odd thing to me, sir,

00:37:23.130 --> 00:37:27.170
something that, well, I can't shake quite loose of.

00:37:27.230 --> 00:37:30.000
He said they were spending more time

00:37:30.120 --> 00:37:38.130
training for seizing and for preventing who set up this outfit well henderson and broderick

00:37:38.130 --> 00:37:44.390
reported directly to general scott so well i assume general scott did sir you assume well

00:37:44.390 --> 00:37:49.410
you work directly under general scott don't you well yes sir but well i guess i'd been

00:37:49.410 --> 00:37:54.100
cut out for some security reason go ahead colonel

00:38:01.240 --> 00:38:05.350
This is General Hardesty's writing. I know it pretty well.

00:38:05.350 --> 00:38:09.040
That paper came from the Joint Chief's meeting room.

00:38:09.040 --> 00:38:12.730
I can't make much out of this scrawl.

00:38:12.730 --> 00:38:18.270
Air Lift EcomCon, 40 K-212s at Site Y by 0700 Sunday.

00:38:18.270 --> 00:38:21.010
Chai, New York, LA, Utah.

00:38:21.010 --> 00:38:22.010
K-212?

00:38:22.010 --> 00:38:25.630
Air Force Jet Transport, sir.

00:38:25.630 --> 00:38:26.590
What do you make of it?

00:38:26.590 --> 00:38:29.830
Well, they're obviously scheduled to lift this whole command out of Site Y

00:38:30.000 --> 00:38:33.460
That's what Henderson called the base near El Paso, before the alert Sunday, and take

00:38:33.460 --> 00:38:36.600
those troops to Chicago, Los Angeles, New York, and Utah.

00:38:36.600 --> 00:38:38.300
Well, why Utah?

00:38:38.300 --> 00:38:41.480
Telephone company has big relay facilities for its long lines in Utah.

00:38:41.480 --> 00:38:43.320
Precisely, what are you leading up to?

00:38:43.320 --> 00:38:49.950
Well, I'm not certain, Mr. President, but, well, let me try to tell you the other things

00:38:49.950 --> 00:38:53.540
that have happened the past two days.

00:38:53.540 --> 00:38:57.870
General Scott has some kind of pool going on the Preakness race which runs on Sunday.

00:38:57.870 --> 00:39:00.000
He sent messages to every important field.

00:39:00.000 --> 00:39:03.770
the field commander talking about getting their bets in on time.

00:39:03.770 --> 00:39:08.720
Admiral Barneswell was the only one who sent in a no-bet message.

00:39:08.720 --> 00:39:16.660
Your General Scott's interest in horses isn't classified, General.

00:39:16.660 --> 00:39:20.200
I don't think those messages had anything to do with horses, sir.

00:39:20.200 --> 00:39:22.610
I think it was some kind of a code.

00:39:22.610 --> 00:39:24.580
It's a fair-sized assumption.

00:39:24.580 --> 00:39:27.720
General Scott wanted those messages kept under wraps.

00:39:27.720 --> 00:39:28.720
Under wraps?

00:39:28.720 --> 00:39:30.000
Yes, sir.

00:39:30.000 --> 00:39:37.500
decoded those messages as being shipped out to Hawaii. There are other things, Mr. President.

00:39:37.500 --> 00:39:42.850
Last night at a party at Stuart Diller's house. You were there, Paul. Yes, sir. Senator Prentiss

00:39:42.850 --> 00:39:47.870
indicated to me a knowledge of the alert. No one on the hill is supposed to know about

00:39:47.870 --> 00:39:50.790
that alert. Senator Prentiss knows, and General Scott

00:39:50.790 --> 00:39:55.800
knows that he knows. That's a hell of an assumption. How do you know that? The general lied. He said

00:39:55.800 --> 00:40:00.000
he was in bed last night at 8 o'clock, but I went to his quarters at Fort Myer right after the party because

00:40:00.000 --> 00:40:02.260
I was concerned that Senator Prentice had found out about the alert.

00:40:03.290 --> 00:40:04.470
Well, the general wasn't in bed.

00:40:04.570 --> 00:40:07.470
He was with Senator Prentice, who arrived at his house at 11.45.

00:40:08.210 --> 00:40:09.310
And that's all?

00:40:10.370 --> 00:40:12.830
Well, Congress recessed yesterday,

00:40:13.150 --> 00:40:16.330
and Vice President Giannelli's in Italy on a goodwill tour,

00:40:16.390 --> 00:40:18.850
and this Sunday you're going to be at an underground command post

00:40:18.850 --> 00:40:20.450
on Mount Thunder completely alone.

00:40:20.820 --> 00:40:22.780
You won't even have press people in attendance.

00:40:23.230 --> 00:40:23.830
It's true.

00:40:25.400 --> 00:40:27.000
General Scott asked that I come alone.

00:40:28.500 --> 00:40:29.220
All right, Colonel.

00:40:29.220 --> 00:40:29.480
All right.

00:40:31.050 --> 00:40:34.750
Let's sum it up, shall we?

00:40:34.750 --> 00:40:35.920
You're suggesting what?

00:40:35.920 --> 00:40:39.370
I'm not sure, Mr. President.

