Murkowski air defense. He's screaming bloody murder about those 12 troop carriers dispatched to El Paso.

01:30:05.830 --> 01:30:11.220
Says they're checked for El Paso and then lost on the radar screen. He wants to know where they went and why.

01:30:11.420 --> 01:30:16.140
He also wants to know why 30 more are at Bragg with the same destination.

01:30:16.140 --> 01:30:17.190
What did you tell him?

01:30:17.190 --> 01:30:20.170
I told him it was classified and forget it.

01:30:20.170 --> 01:30:21.170
Well, that ought to do it.

01:30:21.170 --> 01:30:21.970
It's him.

01:30:21.970 --> 01:30:30.000
He's a hard-nosed book player with a radar screen at his bed. If I know him, he's not gonna stop here.

01:30:30.220 --> 01:30:33.440
right up to the president.

01:30:33.440 --> 01:30:35.040
- Go ahead, Barney.

01:30:35.040 --> 01:30:36.520
- One of my controllers was watching

01:30:36.520 --> 01:30:37.920
a flight of troop carriers,

01:30:37.920 --> 01:30:40.010
Wednesday night, heading for El Paso.

01:30:40.010 --> 01:30:42.870
They turned northwest and dropped off our radar screens.

01:30:42.870 --> 01:30:46.110
Now, we both tried to find out about it through channels,

01:30:46.110 --> 01:30:48.270
and all we get is the big stall.

01:30:48.270 --> 01:30:51.230
There's some kind of a secret base out there, Mr. President,

01:30:51.230 --> 01:30:54.570
and I think I should have been notified of it.

01:30:54.570 --> 01:30:55.900
- Keep going, General.

01:30:55.900 --> 01:30:57.300
- 30 more of these transports

01:30:57.300 --> 01:31:00.000
were due at this classified place at 0700.

01:31:00.000 --> 01:31:13.820
7 a.m. tomorrow. Now I learn it's been moved up to 2300 tonight. General, I want all those aircraft

01:31:13.820 --> 01:31:19.770
grounded. You're to give the order that they're to stand down. You may say that's been authorized

01:31:19.770 --> 01:31:25.080
by the president, can be verified by phoning the White House. You understand that? I guess I do,

01:31:25.080 --> 01:31:29.640
sir. I want you available. Phone in, let this office know where you are.

01:31:30.090 --> 01:31:30.590
Yes, sir.

01:31:33.990 --> 01:31:36.140
The next step should be to your liking, Chris.

01:31:37.860 --> 01:31:40.160
Esther, call the Pentagon.

01:31:41.660 --> 01:31:43.420
Tell General Scott I want to see him right away.

01:31:43.620 --> 01:31:44.000
Yes, sir.

01:31:44.000 --> 01:31:46.120
I think it's time we face the enemy, Mr. President.

01:31:47.530 --> 01:31:48.310
He's not the enemy.

01:31:49.490 --> 01:31:55.100
Scott, the Joint Chiefs, even the very emotional, very illogical, lunatic fringe, they're not the enemy.

01:31:56.900 --> 01:32:00.000
The enemy's an age, a nuclear war.

01:32:00.000 --> 01:32:09.390
age it happens to kill man's faith and his ability to influence what happens to him and

01:32:09.390 --> 01:32:15.210
out of this comes a sickness a sickness of frustration a feeling of impotence helplessness

01:32:15.210 --> 01:32:25.210
weakness and from this this desperation we look for a champion in red white and blue every now

01:32:25.210 --> 01:32:30.000
and then a man on a white horse rides by and we appoint him to be our personal god for the duration

01:32:31.470 --> 01:32:33.390
For some men, it was a Senator McCarthy.

01:32:34.250 --> 01:32:36.030
For others, it was a General Walker.

01:32:37.200 --> 01:32:39.450
Now it's a General Scott.

01:33:06.970 --> 01:33:11.810
- General Scott is here, sir.

01:33:11.810 --> 01:33:22.850
- Send him in, please.

01:33:22.850 --> 01:33:23.620
- Sit down, General.

01:33:33.930 --> 01:33:37.120
I'm glad, sir, you've decided to call off that fishing trip.

01:33:37.120 --> 01:33:40.260
Don't bother about that.

01:33:40.260 --> 01:33:43.950
We don't need it tonight.

01:33:43.950 --> 01:33:47.890
We aren't going to have an alert tomorrow.

01:33:47.890 --> 01:33:52.830
I beg your pardon, Mr. President.

01:33:52.830 --> 01:33:54.220
You wish the alert canceled?

01:33:54.220 --> 01:33:55.420
I do.

01:33:55.420 --> 01:33:57.600
I intend to cancel it.

01:33:57.600 --> 01:33:59.220
May I ask why?

01:34:00.540 --> 01:34:02.460
- Certain facts have come to my attention lately.

01:34:02.460 --> 01:34:05.550
I won't waste time by detailing them all now.

01:34:05.550 --> 01:34:09.070
I'll simply say that I want your resignation tonight,

01:34:09.070 --> 01:34:10.950
and those of Generals Horesty, Riley,

01:34:10.950 --> 01:34:19.300
and Diefenbach as well.

01:34:19.300 --> 01:34:20.260
- Joking, Mr. President,

01:34:20.260 --> 01:34:22.720
'til you've taken leave of your senses.

01:34:22.720 --> 01:34:24.760
I know of no reason why I should remove my name

01:34:24.760 --> 01:34:26.870
from the active list voluntarily,

01:34:26.870 --> 01:34:29.380
or for that matter, any of the other Joint Chiefs.

01:34:29.380 --> 01:34:30.000
- You could get it!

01:34:30.000 --> 01:34:35.440
Give me the reasons, General, but if you want me to itemize them, I should be glad to do so.

01:34:35.440 --> 01:34:36.640
Please do.

01:34:36.640 --> 01:34:43.670
You have used, without my authority, substantial sums from the Joint Chiefs Contingency Fund

01:34:43.670 --> 01:34:48.210
to establish a base and to train a special unit of troops whose purpose and even whose

01:34:48.210 --> 01:34:54.120
existence was kept secret from me, from responsible officials of the Bureau of the Budget, and

01:34:54.120 --> 01:34:55.520
members of the Congress.

01:34:55.520 --> 01:34:56.890
And the name of that unit?

01:34:56.890 --> 01:34:58.970
You know the unit.

01:34:58.970 --> 01:35:00.000
Its designation is E.C.

01:35:00.090 --> 01:35:03.970
- Come, Con.

01:35:03.970 --> 01:35:06.630
- I'm afraid your memory fails you, Mr. President.

01:35:06.630 --> 01:35:08.250
You gave me verbal authorization

01:35:08.250 --> 01:35:10.380
for the base and the unit.

01:35:10.380 --> 01:35:12.520
As I recall it, we covered quite a few items that day.

01:35:12.520 --> 01:35:14.730
Perhaps you didn't pay much attention to this.

01:35:14.730 --> 01:35:16.110
I merely assumed you'd informed

01:35:16.110 --> 01:35:17.230
the director of the budget.

01:35:17.230 --> 01:35:19.830
- What was the date of that meeting, General?

01:35:19.830 --> 01:35:21.540
- I can't recall exactly,

01:35:21.540 --> 01:35:23.390
but it was right here in this office.

01:35:23.390 --> 01:35:24.950
Last fall, November, I believe.

01:35:24.950 --> 01:35:27.750
- You have a record of the date and subject?

01:35:27.750 --> 01:35:28.960
- Well, certainly, Mr. President.

01:35:30.000 --> 01:35:34.280
my office. Well, if you care to make a point of it, I'll drive over to the Pentagon right now and

01:35:34.280 --> 01:35:39.820
get it. That won't be necessary, General. No, it won't be necessary. Colonel Murdoch, my aide,

01:35:39.840 --> 01:35:45.670
is outside. He sat in on the meeting. He will substantiate my memorandum as to the date and

01:35:45.670 --> 01:35:52.860
the discussion. I'll ask him in. That won't be necessary either, General. You kept a member of

01:35:52.860 --> 01:35:57.760
the United States Senate forcibly detained at this base, and he will so testify. And that would be?

01:35:57.760 --> 01:35:59.800
That would be Senator Raymond Clark.

01:36:00.220 --> 01:36:02.640
the senior senator from Georgia.

01:36:02.640 --> 01:36:04.020
- I wasn't aware that Senator Clark

01:36:04.020 --> 01:36:05.830
had ever visited the base.

01:36:05.830 --> 01:36:09.060
- He will also testify as to the collusion

01:36:09.060 --> 01:36:10.420
between the commander of the base

01:36:10.420 --> 01:36:12.620
and one Senator Frederick Prentiss of California,

01:36:12.620 --> 01:36:14.700
who with yourself and only a handful of others

01:36:14.700 --> 01:36:24.500
knew of the existence of the base.

01:36:24.500 --> 01:36:25.950
- Any other charges, Mr. President?

01:36:25.950 --> 01:36:30.000
- Would you like them in chronological order?

01:36:30.000 --> 01:36:32.590
of a commanding officer for a secret base

01:36:32.590 --> 01:36:35.930
who is openly contemptuous of civilian authority

01:36:35.930 --> 01:36:37.570
and who has made some statements that come close

01:36:37.570 --> 01:36:39.290
to violations of the sedition laws.

01:36:39.290 --> 01:36:42.480
- Mr. President, I never discuss politics with my officers,

01:36:42.480 --> 01:36:44.940
but I do demand the highest competence.

01:36:44.940 --> 01:36:46.780
And Colonel Broderick is an excellent officer

01:36:46.780 --> 01:36:48.450
with a fine combat record.

01:36:48.450 --> 01:36:51.480
- And an interesting travel record, you might add.

01:36:51.480 --> 01:36:53.180
What, for example, was he doing the other day

01:36:53.180 --> 01:36:54.800
on a motorboat, cruising around my island

01:36:54.800 --> 01:36:55.640
at Blue Lake, Maine?

01:36:55.640 --> 01:36:58.240
And don't tell me that's a figment of my imagination

01:36:58.240 --> 01:36:59.600
because I've got him on film.

01:37:00.000 --> 01:37:03.000
of Colonel William Henderson at Dulles Airport early this morning.

01:37:03.000 --> 01:37:05.000
I know about that case, Mr. President.

01:37:05.000 --> 01:37:07.880
Colonel Henderson struck an enlisted man and left his post.

01:37:07.880 --> 01:37:10.060
He's now being held for disciplinary action.

01:37:10.060 --> 01:37:14.440
Incommunicado, you might add, so that he doesn't tell what he knows.

01:37:14.440 --> 01:37:18.610
Then there are the wagering activities of yours, General.

01:37:18.610 --> 01:37:20.880
Particularly a betting pool on the Preakness.

01:37:20.880 --> 01:37:22.880
Oh, come now, Mr. President.

01:37:22.880 --> 01:37:26.950
Or perhaps more aptly classified your personal and private code.

01:37:26.950 --> 01:37:30.000
It covers your plans for a long time.

01:37:30.000 --> 01:37:33.260
for the military overthrow of the United States government.

01:37:34.230 --> 01:37:36.970
I presume, Mr. President, you're prepared to back up that charge?

01:37:37.480 --> 01:37:40.600
I am prepared to brand you for what you are, General.

01:37:41.820 --> 01:37:45.020
A strutting egoist with a Napoleonic power complex

01:37:45.020 --> 01:37:47.270
and an out-and-out traitor.

01:37:49.380 --> 01:37:51.340
I know you think I'm a weak sister, General,

01:37:52.140 --> 01:37:53.820
but when it comes to my oath of office,

01:37:54.340 --> 01:37:55.700
and depending the Constitution of the United States...

01:37:55.700 --> 01:37:57.170
Nobody has to teach me how to salute a flag.

01:37:57.170 --> 01:37:59.350
Somebody has to teach you about the democratic processes

01:37:59.350 --> 01:38:00.000
that that flag

01:38:00.090 --> 01:38:02.920
- But don't you presume to take on that job, Mr. President.

01:38:02.920 --> 01:38:04.890
Because frankly, you're not qualified.

01:38:04.890 --> 01:38:06.210
Your course of action in the past year

01:38:06.210 --> 01:38:08.200
has bordered on criminal negligence.

01:38:08.200 --> 01:38:09.220
This treaty with the Russians

01:38:09.220 --> 01:38:12.180
is a violation of any concept of security.

01:38:12.180 --> 01:38:14.160
You're not a weak sister, Mr. President.

01:38:14.160 --> 01:38:18.100
You're a criminally weak sister.

01:38:18.100 --> 01:38:19.930
And if you want to talk about your oath of office,

01:38:19.930 --> 01:38:22.210
I'm here to tell you face to face, President Lyman,

01:38:22.210 --> 01:38:23.310
that you violated that oath

01:38:23.310 --> 01:38:24.930
when you stripped this country of its muscles,

01:38:24.930 --> 01:38:26.940
when you deliberately played upon the fear and fatigue

01:38:26.940 --> 01:38:29.280
of the people and told them they could remove that fear

01:38:29.280 --> 01:38:30.000
by the stroke of a pen.

01:38:31.050 --> 01:38:35.710
then when this nation rejected you lost its faith in you and began militantly to oppose you you

01:38:35.710 --> 01:38:39.390
violated that oath by simply not resigning from office and turning this country over to someone

01:38:39.390 --> 01:38:44.670
who could represent the people of the united states that would be general james mattoon scott wouldn't

01:38:44.670 --> 01:38:52.970
it i don't know whether to laugh at that kind of megalomania or simply crying james mattoon scott

01:38:52.970 --> 01:38:57.520
as you put it hasn't the slightest interest in his own glorification but he does have an abiding

01:38:57.520 --> 01:39:00.000
concern about the survival of this country then by

01:39:00.000 --> 01:39:02.340
Why, God, run for office!

01:39:02.340 --> 01:39:06.020
You have such a fervid, passionate, evangelical affection for your country.

01:39:06.020 --> 01:39:11.500
Why in the name of God don't you have any faith in the system of government you're so hell-bent to protect?

01:39:11.500 --> 01:39:14.500
You say I've duped the people, General. I've built them. I've misled them.

01:39:14.500 --> 01:39:16.500
I've stripped them naked and made them defenseless.

01:39:16.500 --> 01:39:22.650
You accuse me of having lost their faith, deliberately and criminally shut my ears to the national voice.

01:39:22.650 --> 01:39:23.650
I do.

01:39:23.650 --> 01:39:30.000
Where the hell have you heard that voice, General? In freight elevators?

01:39:30.120 --> 01:39:32.840
In dark alleys? In secret places in the dead of night?

01:39:33.210 --> 01:39:36.120
How did that voice seep into a locked room full of conspirators?

01:39:36.890 --> 01:39:40.490
That's not where you hear the voice of the people, General, not in this republic.

01:39:40.910 --> 01:39:43.010
You want to defend the United States of America,

01:39:43.420 --> 01:39:46.670
then defend it with the tools it supplies you with, its constitution.

01:39:47.270 --> 01:39:49.390
You ask for a mandate, General, from a ballot box.

01:39:50.000 --> 01:39:52.960
You don't steal it after midnight, when the country has its back turned.

01:39:52.960 --> 01:39:54.970
Are you serious, Mr. President?

01:39:56.300 --> 01:39:58.300
Are you honest to God serious?

01:39:59.320 --> 01:40:00.000
Well, I could...

01:40:02.240 --> 01:40:06.450
I'd walk out of here tonight and offer myself as candidate for the Office of Presidency.

01:40:06.450 --> 01:40:11.090
And by tomorrow morning, I'd be sitting at that desk with precisely the mandate you hold so dear.

01:40:11.090 --> 01:40:14.410
And what's more, Mr. President, you know it, and I know it, and this country knows it.

01:40:14.410 --> 01:40:18.060
So don't tell me I'd have seized an office tomorrow without the benefit of support.

01:40:18.060 --> 01:40:22.200
If you really had the guts to call for a show of hands, you'd be on an airplane right now back to Ohio.

01:40:22.200 --> 01:40:24.490
You can ask for and get your show of hands, General.

01:40:24.490 --> 01:40:26.950
Just wait a year and nine months for something called election.

01:40:26.950 --> 01:40:30.000
A year and nine months from now, I don't think there'll be an electorate, let alone an election.

01:40:30.000 --> 01:40:32.720
I think we'll be sitting on our own rubble,

01:40:32.720 --> 01:40:34.740
a minimum of 100 million dead,

01:40:34.740 --> 01:40:37.050
and on the gravestone we can carve.

01:40:37.050 --> 01:40:40.260
They died for Jordan Lyman's concept of peace.

01:40:40.260 --> 01:40:45.810
General! General!

01:41:01.240 --> 01:41:05.910
Did it ever occur to you that if you took over this government by force,

01:41:07.280 --> 01:41:09.500
you wouldn't have to wait a year and nine months for the funeral?

01:41:11.500 --> 01:41:15.280
If the Soviet Union saw our government being taken over by a military dictatorship,

01:41:16.290 --> 01:41:19.130
how long do you suppose it would take them to break the treaty?

01:41:19.830 --> 01:41:21.070
Possibly even attack us?

01:41:22.750 --> 01:41:25.220
I think perhaps a question of days.

01:41:25.800 --> 01:41:26.400
Perhaps hours.

01:41:27.340 --> 01:41:28.040
Certainly weeks.

01:41:32.040 --> 01:41:33.660
I want your resignation, General.

01:41:33.660 --> 01:41:34.560
I want it tonight.

01:41:34.560 --> 01:41:36.180
I'm expecting it.

01:41:36.180 --> 01:41:41.420
Along with the other members of the Joint Chiefs who were involved in this treason.

01:41:41.420 --> 01:41:47.330
I'll tell you quite unequivocally, I'll not tell the reason for your resignation.

01:41:47.330 --> 01:41:51.740
If that were ever made public, this country would go down the drain.

01:41:51.740 --> 01:41:53.460
Will you resign, General?

01:41:53.460 --> 01:41:56.160
I will not resign.

01:41:56.160 --> 01:41:58.470
I can demand your resignation, as you well know.

01:41:58.470 --> 01:42:00.000
Demand and be damned, I will not resign voluntarily.

01:42:00.000 --> 01:42:02.590
Not voluntarily, nor will any of the others.

01:42:02.590 --> 01:42:05.360
But what I will do is take this issue to the people.

01:42:05.360 --> 01:42:07.550
I'll demand a public platform,

01:42:07.550 --> 01:42:08.810
and then we'll see which one of us

01:42:08.810 --> 01:42:18.260
the United States will follow.

01:42:18.260 --> 01:42:26.480
- Anything else, Mr. President?

01:42:26.480 --> 01:42:30.000
- General, I've called a press conference

01:42:30.000 --> 01:42:39.370
for tomorrow i'll announce that i've asked for all of your resignations i'll use as a reason

01:42:39.370 --> 01:42:54.450
our differences over the treaty without proof you couldn't possibly say otherwise

01:42:54.450 --> 01:42:58.640
you simply wouldn't dare i'm going to fight you

01:43:56.270 --> 01:43:59.510
I'm sorry, Jigs. Return them to Miss Holborn.

01:44:35.050 --> 01:44:37.570
This will be delivered at 9 o'clock tonight on all major networks.

01:44:38.040 --> 01:44:39.290
I'll be taping it in one hour.

01:44:41.730 --> 01:44:43.290
This is strong stuff, General. Are you sure...

01:44:43.290 --> 01:44:43.850
Thank you, General.

01:44:47.030 --> 01:44:51.960
You're sure that he won't use this press conference of his to make any accusations?

01:44:52.440 --> 01:44:56.310
He will use this press conference to support a position that is totally indefensible.

01:45:01.020 --> 01:45:06.710
If he accuses us of sedition, whether he has the proof or not, this could be a pretty sticky business.

01:45:06.930 --> 01:45:08.070
Jordan Lyman is finished.

01:45:09.080 --> 01:45:12.040
No matter what he says during his press conference, no matter what he does after,

01:45:13.370 --> 01:45:16.070
an educated guess would be that within a week there'll be a move for his impeachment.

01:45:17.900 --> 01:45:18.520
That's it, gentlemen.

01:45:19.020 --> 01:45:20.840
You're welcome to stay here and watch on television.

01:45:21.240 --> 01:45:21.940
I'll be at the studio.

01:45:22.920 --> 01:45:24.560
Colonel Murdock will be in touch with me if I'm needed.

01:45:25.860 --> 01:45:26.330
Good day.

01:45:36.590 --> 01:45:38.390
Stay tuned for the preakness that follows...

01:45:38.390 --> 01:45:39.590
Stay tuned for a special broadcast.

01:45:39.590 --> 01:45:40.890
This is the NBC television network.

01:45:40.890 --> 01:45:44.510
The president next on the ABC television network.

01:45:44.510 --> 01:45:49.370
Ladies and gentlemen, the president of the United States.

01:45:49.370 --> 01:46:00.000
All right, gentlemen.

01:46:00.000 --> 01:46:05.910
let's begin. Mr. President, the Gallup poll of last week indicated what appears to be a very

01:46:05.910 --> 01:46:10.950
universal rejection of your entire political philosophy, namely, sir, the nuclear treaty with

01:46:10.950 --> 01:46:17.830
the Soviets. Would you care to comment on that? Insofar as the treaty is concerned, my reasons for

01:46:17.830 --> 01:46:24.260
asking that it be ratified have been stated and restated. We have reached a point on this earth

01:46:30.320 --> 01:46:32.620
- Excuse me just a moment, gentlemen.

01:46:34.950 --> 01:46:41.760
- Jordy, you better talk to this fellow.

01:46:41.760 --> 01:46:44.910
- Mr. President, this is Henry Whitney from our embassy in Madrid.

01:46:44.910 --> 01:46:55.590
- Brought this.

01:46:55.590 --> 01:46:57.550
- Mr. President, I'm the only one who's read that paper.

01:46:57.550 --> 01:46:59.440
Nobody knows I'm here.

01:47:00.570 --> 01:47:03.870
- Delay the press conference for half an hour.

01:47:03.870 --> 01:47:06.410
You are never to disclose or even hint

01:47:06.410 --> 01:47:08.490
at the existence of this paper, Mr. Whitney.

01:47:08.490 --> 01:47:10.370
I emphasize the word never.

01:47:10.370 --> 01:47:11.590
Ray, have this photo status.

01:47:11.590 --> 01:47:12.430
- Yes, sir.

01:47:12.430 --> 01:47:13.330
- Thank you, Mr. Whitney.

01:47:13.330 --> 01:47:14.120
- Yes, sir.

01:47:14.120 --> 01:47:15.660
- Colonel Casey, see that Scott and the others

01:47:15.660 --> 01:47:17.010
get copies right away.

01:47:17.010 --> 01:47:17.530
- Yes, sir.

01:47:38.670 --> 01:47:46.120
- That's a signed statement from Admiral Barnswell.

01:47:46.120 --> 01:47:47.420
- Nightcrawler, Colonel.

01:47:47.420 --> 01:47:50.070
Pedlar, you sell information.

01:47:50.070 --> 01:47:51.370
Are you sufficiently up on your Bible

01:47:51.370 --> 01:47:56.090
to know who Judas was?

01:47:56.090 --> 01:47:58.490
- I suggest you read that letter, sir.

01:47:58.490 --> 01:48:00.000
It's from the President.

01:48:03.480 --> 01:48:05.860
- Are you ordering me to answer, sir? - I am.

01:48:05.860 --> 01:48:11.770
Yes, I know who Judas was.

